WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Good morning, John! I'm back, and I'm officially a dad!

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.380
Which means that I can make a video that I've wanted to make for years,

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.000
but did not feel qualified, until this moment.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.060
This... is 41 dad jokes, in under 4 minutes.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.720
Now that I have a son, you might say I have a "dad bod", but I'd rather call it a "father figure."

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.700
I don't know if you know this, but I can cut through wood just by looking at it.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.280
Yeah, I didn't believe it at first either, but I saw it with my own eyes.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.640
You know what the loneliest cheese is?

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.620
Provolone.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.700
Also, did you hear about the explosion at the cheese factory?

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.360
Yeah, it was terrible. The only thing left was the brie (debris).

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.320
I just found out my friend was dating a communist. He really should've noticed, there were so many red flags.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.860
To the man who stole my thesaurus, I have NO WORDS for how angry I am!

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.080
You know, I've always hated elevators, which is why I've recently started taking steps to avoid them.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.700
Hey, how long is dinner gonna be?

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.340
Oh, uh like, th—this long?

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:52.460
You know, I like to wear these leather shoes when I'm sneaking around at night.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.360
'Cause they are literally made of hide.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:59.760
I cannot wait for my son to one day say to me: "Dad, I think I have your sense of humor."

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.660
So that I can say to him: "You give that back!"

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.360
So, why do scuba divers fall backwards out of boats?

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:07.240
'Cause if they fell forward, they'd still be in the boat.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.100
Hank 1: "Alright, uh, what are you doing?"

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.700
Hank 2: "I'm looking for Will Smith. He always leaves Fresh Prints."

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.660
I love how the Earth rotates; it really makes my day.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:17.920
Hey, how does dinner smell?

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.140
Through its nose I guess?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.340
Feeling cranky, baby?

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:21.580
There's a nap (an app) for that!

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.780
You know, I don't like Russian dolls. They are so full of themselves!

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.460
Hank 1: *Laughs*

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:29.740
Hank 2: Dude, what is so funny?

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.980
H1: Oh, I'm just looking at mountain ranges on Google Images. They are hill areas!

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.900
Oh, boiling water. You will be mist!

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:38.960
You know, I've realized that— *baby crying sound*

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.440
Aww, are you resisting arrest?

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.700
That's okay. I don't want them to accuse me of kidnapping.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.480
Orion's Belt. Huge waste of space.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.920
Get it? Like waist of space?

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.320
Yeah, I know I get it. It's not a great joke. I give it 3 stars.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.440
Aww.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:01.020
You're done with your nap? This is my baby.

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.400
Hey, how you doing?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.360
Okay, we're gonna take you to mommy, sorry.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:11.940
What's Whitney Houston's favorite type of coordination? Hand eeeyyyeee.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.280
Hank 1: What're you doing? What are you doing?

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.160
Hank 2: I'm uh, measuring your patience. Ow!

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.980
What do you get when you divide a poop into three pieces? Turds! You get turds!

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.860
How many sides does a circle have?

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.420
That is actually a really interesting ques—

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.520
Two! The outside and the inside.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:30.260
Man, can I eat a quesadilla right now.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:33.540
A whole case? Why don't you just start from one "dilla" and see how you feel from there?

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.840
Hey, how's the temperature out there?

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.220
It's pretty nice, you only need like a jean jacket.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.660
Oh, so it's in the 80s?

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:40.180
What did Barack Obama say when he dropped his shell at the beach?

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.520
"Oh no! My shell!"

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.140
That's my Barack Obama impersonation. I've been working on it.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.180
So, these two pharaohs, they farted at the same time.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.360
Yeah, they had a toot In common.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.600
Oh, son, I'm glad I'm not your math book. It has got so many problems!

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.120
What's the difference between a roast beef and pea soup?

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.140
Anybody can roast beef.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.880
[Awkward silence]

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.700
How do locomotives know where to go? They go through lots of training.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.860
Hey you know where you can get chicken stock in bulk?

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.480
Yeah. The stock market.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.720
Hank 1: Hey, what are you reading?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.100
Hank 2: This? It's a mystery.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.900
Hank 1: I mean, doesn't it say right on the cover?

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.960
One time I was at this really skeezy bus stop and there was a lobster with boobs.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.140
Yeah, it was a busty crustacean at a crusty bus station.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.700
Hank 1: Hey, do you serve fish here?

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.600
Hank 2: Yeah, we do.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.660
Hank 1: Excellent, Dave will have the steak.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.380
Oh, man, there's a hole in my shoe.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.320
It's how I get my foot in it.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:27.280
John, it was a real pat on the back for me when Organic Valley decided they were gonna sculpt me out of butter.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:28.780
It was a dairy big deal for me.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:30.300
It was a churning point in my life.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:32.100
I... think it made me a butter man.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.280
That actually is a thing that happened. Organic Valley sculpted me out of butter

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.780
because people voted on Twitter enough.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.180
And finally, you know what my very first dad joke of dadhood was?

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.120
We were headed out, and he needed a new diaper, and so I was like, "I'm gonna change him real quick."

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.800
I put him on the changing table and I said, "Now what am I gonna change you into? A rhinoceros?"

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:50.660
And I was like, yes! I'm a dad! I made an embarrassing joke, and I got peed on, and I'm officially

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:53.540
a dad and I love it! John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:58.160
I cannot believe how many jokes videos I've made over the years. You can watch all of them, I made a playlist.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.560
Boop de de boop do doo, bop!

